WEBVTT

00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:12.606
Charged twice.

00:00:14.457 --> 00:00:16.249
A shopper presses Place order twice.

00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:17.828
Is the card charged twice?

00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:19.082
Mostly no:

00:00:19.364 --> 00:00:21.070
the order system refuses an identical

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:22.222
order placed within minutes.

00:00:22.862 --> 00:00:24.953
In sixteen days, it did that more than

00:00:24.996 --> 00:00:25.934
eight hundred times.

00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:30.695
So how does a double charge happen?

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.425
The ways we have found share one cause:

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.241
a program charges again without first asking:

00:00:36.839 --> 00:00:37.905
is this already paid?

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:42.293
Three ways we have measured.

00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:44.810
An order paid with two cards is cancelled,

00:00:45.024 --> 00:00:46.602
and the first card stays charged.

00:00:47.114 --> 00:00:49.290
A rebill is declined, the customer pays

00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:51.551
another way, and the retry charges the old

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:52.294
order too.

00:00:52.411 --> 00:00:54.544
And one subscription is billed twice by

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.287
the order system.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.393
Take the retry.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.569
It used to charge the old order without looking.

00:01:02.252 --> 00:01:04.086
Since the tenth of November it looks first:

00:01:04.598 --> 00:01:06.476
is there a newer paid order for this subscription?

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.481
If there is, it charges nothing.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.280
One guard turned out too blunt.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.054
A gateway check refused any charge on the

00:01:16.096 --> 00:01:17.888
same card for the same amount within

00:01:18.059 --> 00:01:18.759
twenty minutes.

00:01:19.123 --> 00:01:20.915
This year it stopped about three hundred

00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:23.049
double charges, and refused nearly

00:01:23.177 --> 00:01:25.523
seventeen hundred real orders to do it.

00:01:25.822 --> 00:01:27.912
At the end of October it was switched off.

00:01:31.344 --> 00:01:33.136
What finds the rest is a daily watch.

00:01:33.776 --> 00:01:35.440
Every morning it looks for cards left

00:01:35.526 --> 00:01:36.891
charged on cancelled orders,

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.366
and for orders charged again after a retry.

00:01:40.006 --> 00:01:41.883
And when it finds one, a person keeps

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.400
exactly one charge, and sends the other back.

00:01:46.703 --> 00:01:47.403
Charged twice:

00:01:47.727 --> 00:01:50.073
it starts when a program does not look first.

00:01:50.628 --> 00:01:52.505
So look first, watch every morning,

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:54.825
and keep exactly one charge.

